{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Upon me be your curse, my son.</b> There is nothing for you or me to fear from the curse, for I am certain, as HaShem said: ורב יעבד צעיר. Another interpretation: even if he is moved to curse you, he will not curse you, for he will understand on his own that you did not do this knowingly but rather at my instruction, for I am accustomed to stand before him and I put this deceit upon you; and if he comes to curse, let him curse me. Another interpretation: <b>upon me be your curse, my son</b> — in the same manner as על עמך ברכתך (cf. ״upon your people be your blessing״), for why should he curse you when you are bringing him delicacies? Rather, upon me be the curse for you, since you refuse my command. But heed me and go take for me."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:15.566604334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}